WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.369
-Republicans are rushing
to a place retiring

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.638
Supreme Court Justice
Anthony Kennedy

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.708
while simultaneously working to
stop the Russian investigation.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.010
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:15.715
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:18.117
Trump held yet another
campaign rally last night

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.186
in North Dakota,
his third rally in a week.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:23.889
Now, we've been calling these
rallies public therapy sessions,

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:26.859
but it was never more true
than it was last night.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.562
Watch as Trump airs
his deepest insecurities

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.099
about not being seen
as smart, rich, or popular.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.601
-I meet these people.
They call them the elite.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.070
These people.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.940
I look at them,
I say, "That's elite?"

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.109
We got more money.
We got more brains.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.977
We got better houses,
apartments.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.312
We got nicer boats.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.682
We're smarter than they are,
and they say the elite.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.817
We're the elite!

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.385
And I thought
that was so brilliant.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:56.355
I said, "Oh, I am so smart.
I am the smartest person."

00:00:56.355 --> 00:01:00.526
My uncle was a great professor
at MIT for 40 years.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.761
Can you believe?
40 years.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.729
I said,
"But I'm smarter than him.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.364
I'm smarter than anybody."

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.266
A thing comes out, a big poll,
and a couple of polls,

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:11.270
a number of polls that
he's the most powerful,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.840
most popular Republican
in the history of the party.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.577
-Oh, my God, dude,
get a therapist.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.214
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:25.818
I know they're cheap,
but get a therapist.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:30.890
Trump is like a guy at a bar
who acts as his own wingman.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.358
"My buddy thinks you're cute.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:36.095
He's smart and handsome
and popular, and he's me."

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.764
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.566
But you know what Trump says --
he's smarter than anybody,

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.768
and he had a chance
to show off those smarts

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:46.739
while talking about the complex
issue of trade during his rally.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.174
Trump was defending his tariffs.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.709
Now, this is Trump's thing.
It's his big issue,

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.612
the thing he claims
to be an expert on,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.814
yet when his aides
slipped him a note

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.349
during the rally
about Canadian wheat practices,

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.051
he seemed confused.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:00.953
-I'll tell you, John and Kevin
gave me something --

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.154
they just told me --

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:07.994
Canadian wheat markets
consistently discriminate

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:13.433
against the United States wheat
by grading it as feed.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.700
Do you know what that means?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.802
They know what it means.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.936
I don't know
what the hell it means.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.771
I just know it's a bad deal.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.006
What the hell does that mean?
Yeah.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:23.176
-Great, that clears it up.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.610
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.779
Also, he yells out
"Canadian wheat"

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.648
like he's guessing
in Pictionary.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.082
"Canadian wheat!"

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:39.692
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.228
Only Trump could brag
that he's smarter than anybody,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.396
and then, in the same speech,

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.297
admit that he has no idea
what he's talking about.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:48.234
He's like a doctor looking
down at you before surgery

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.568
and says, "Don't worry.

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:51.270
I'm the best surgeon
in the world.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.573
Now just tell me, uh,
what does a kidney look like?"

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.308
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.010
And while he was nursing
his various obsessions,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.544
Trump decided
to return to another one,

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:01.280
perhaps his greatest obsession,
Hillary Clinton,

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.784
during a rant, comparing the
size of his crowds to hers.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.620
-If crooked Hillary
would've won this election,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.224
and if she came here, which is
about a zero percent chance,

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:14.527
after the election,
she'd have 200 people

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.762
in a conference room
in a small hotel.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:20.933
And let me tell you,
if our opponent,

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.402
our wonderful opponent,

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.271
when is she gonna get over it?

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.641
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.711
When does she get over it?

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.812
-When is "she"
gonna get over it?

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:35.248
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.250
If you're still
asking that question

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.753
20 months after the election
you won,

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.522
you're the person
who's not over it.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:45.858
Trump's like a guy
texting his ex two years

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.995
after they broke up, "Why can't
you stop thinking about me?"

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:55.567
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:59.005
While Trump is obsessing
over Hillary or his popularity,

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.540
he also seems to have found
a new hobby horse --

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.409
how much --
Bear with me here.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:07.146
How much rich guys love rockets.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.349
He's mentioned it multiple times
just in the last week,

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.184
while discussing
his plans for NASA,

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.520
including twice yesterday.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.123
-I said, listen,
you got rich guys,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.292
for whatever reason,
they love rockets.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:23.296
I said, "Lease them the land.
Charge them a lot.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.364
But let's do it that way.
That's a lot better.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:26.632
We're like a landlord."

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:29.235
We have all these rich guys,
they love rockets.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:33.373
They're all sending up --
Bezos and Elon Musk

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:36.008
and all of them,
they love the rocket business.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.677
Let them --
Just rent it to them

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.578
for a lot of money
and let them play.

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:41.113
You know, they need our land.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.281
It's good to be
in the real-estate business.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.716
They need our land.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.152
You know, we have these rich
guys, they love these rockets.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.821
I said, "Lease them the land.
Charge them a lot.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.189
They just want to send rockets."

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.692
But I look at it with Bezos,
with Elon Musk --

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.461
they all love rockets.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.765
-He sounds like a stand-up comic
trying out a new bit.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:04:59.932
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:03.069
"What's the deal
with rich guys and rockets?!"

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:07.272
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:11.477
Seriously, though, why on Earth

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.946
would anyone want
their own personal rocket?

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.215
I mean, sure,
things are bad right now,

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.150
but it's not like
anyone actually wishes

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.654
they could blast themselves
into outer space, right?

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.557
-We're following
major breaking news --

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:27.693
President Trump getting another
opportunity to put his stamp

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.461
on the United States
Supreme Court

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.430
for decades to come.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.798
Justice Anthony Kennedy

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.133
announcing his retirement
a few hours ago.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.468
-Hey, honey, it's me.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:39.004
Uh, meet me at the launch pad
in T-minus 20 minutes.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:40.539
No, don't bring the dog!

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:50.249
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.518
So Donald
"Little Rocket Man" Trump

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.753
will now have the chance
to nominate

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.222
a second Supreme Court Justice

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.558
who will shape the future of
everything from gay rights

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.026
to voting rights to Roe v. Wade.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:01.360
Trump, of course, is elated

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.729
that he gets to pick a second
Supreme Court Justice

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.164
who could help
cement his legacy.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.498
And he made that clear yesterday

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.434
when he was meeting
with the president of Portugal.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.571
But right off the bat,
he had to go and make it weird.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.607
-If you don't mind, I'll
just make a quick statement.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:17.109
A man I also
have great respect for,

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.978
Justice Anthony --

00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:21.346
You know
who I'm talking about --

00:06:21.346 --> 00:06:25.250
Justice Kennedy
will be retiring.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.053
-He definitely forgot Kennedy's
last name for a second.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:29.388
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:36.629
"Justice Anthony --
you know who I'm talking about.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:40.265
Old guy, glasses.

00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:44.103
You know him, black robe."

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.638
How do you forget
the name Kennedy?

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:48.641
It's one of the most famous
names in American history.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.009
Is that why Trump puts his names
on all his buildings,

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:52.845
so he won't forget it?

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:57.850
My name is Donald --
Donald...Tower.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.453
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:06.992
-Now, if you remember,
Republicans stole

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:09.161
a Supreme Court seat
from President Obama

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:12.031
by staging an unprecedented
blockade of Obama's choice

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.699
to fill the seat,
Merrick Garland.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.834
They claimed back then
that the American people

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.903
should get to weigh in during
the presidential election,

00:07:17.903 --> 00:07:20.873
which was, at the time,
nine months away.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:23.609
-The American people should
be afforded the opportunity

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:24.877
to weigh in.

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.178
-We think
that the American people

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:28.247
need a chance
to weigh in on this issue.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:32.351
-It ought to be put off, out
of this toxic arena right now

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.753
and put off
until after the election.

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:37.890
-This should be a decision
for the people, George.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.425
Let the election decide it.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.594
-Let's let
the American people decide.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.362
-There you go -- McConnell said,
"Let the people decide."

00:07:44.362 --> 00:07:46.298
So now that we're four months
away from an election,

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:48.167
I'm sure McConnell,
a man of his word,

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.369
will follow the rule he made up
and hold off the vote

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.238
until after the election.
And I'm just kidding.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:53.739
McConnell is totally
full of [bleep]

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.908
-We will vote to confirm

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:59.712
Justice Kennedy's
successor this fall.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.780
It's imperative that
the president's nominee

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.449
be considered fairly.

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:04.817
-Considered fairly?

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.786
You refused to even meet
with Merrick Garland.

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:09.055
Look at that sweet man.

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:12.792
That's like refusing to pet
a Golden Retriever.

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:15.962
"No, thank you.
I prefer a rattlesnake."

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:18.130
[ Laughter ]

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.833
"I'd like to pet
a good ol' rattlesnake."

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:24.069
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:26.839
"Come here now.
N-Nice snake."

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:29.842
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.777
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:36.381
Here's the lesson.

00:08:36.381 --> 00:08:39.384
The GOP isn't operating
on arguments or principles.

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:41.787
They don't care about being
called hypocrites or liars.

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.289
Hypocrisy isn't their weakness,
it's their platform.

00:08:44.289 --> 00:08:47.025
We saw that yet again during a
Congressional hearing

00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:48.560
on the Russia investigation
today.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.596
Remember, Republicans
spent millions of dollars

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.464
over four years
investigating Benghazis

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:53.699
and came up with nothing.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.200
And yet today,
they basically yelled

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.936
at Deputy Attorney General
Rod Rosenstein

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:58.337
to end the Russia investigation.

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:01.940
Here's retiring GOP Congressman
Trey Gowdy freaking out

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.442
at Rosenstein today.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.344
-We're two years
into this investigation,

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:06.412
we're a year and a half
into the presidency,

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:10.149
we're over a year
into Special Counsel.

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:11.817
There is a presumption of guilt.

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:13.886
There's a desire
by Democrat Senators

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:16.421
to fundraise
off of your investigation.

00:09:16.421 --> 00:09:19.224
More than 60 Democrats
have already voted to proceed

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:20.926
with impeachment
before Bob Mueller

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:24.596
has found a single,
solitary damn thing!

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:28.367
More than 60 have voted to
move forward with impeachment!

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:31.136
And he hasn't
presented his first finding!

00:09:31.136 --> 00:09:33.139
If you have evidence
of wrongdoing

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:36.008
by any member
of the Trump campaign,

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:38.744
present it
to the damn grand jury.

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:42.815
Whatever you got,
finish it the hell up.

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:44.116
-What's up with Trey Gowdy?

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:47.219
I mean, look at him --
loose tie, messy hair.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.755
He looks like he's about
to be cut off by the bartender.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.624
"They're trying to impeach him!"

00:09:51.624 --> 00:09:59.899
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:02.168
Of course Gowdy's the same guy
who dragged Hillary Clinton

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:04.637
in front of a committee to
testify about Benghazi

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:06.739
during
the presidential campaign.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.607
And even he admitted
after that hearing

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:10.242
that he didn't
learn anything new.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:13.178
-Well, when you say knew today,
we knew some of that already.

00:10:13.178 --> 00:10:14.613
We knew about the e-mails.

00:10:14.613 --> 00:10:18.116
In terms of her testimony,
I don't know that she testified

00:10:18.116 --> 00:10:20.652
that much differently today
than she has previous times

00:10:20.652 --> 00:10:22.288
she's testified, so...

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:24.490
I'd have to go back
and look at the transcript.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.891
-Go back
and look at the transcript?

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:28.494
Even the transcript
would be fed up.

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.396
[ Laughter ]

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:35.534
Establishment Democrats
need to learn that Republicans

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:36.969
don't care
about being hypocrites.

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:38.370
It's just raw politics.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.506
Trump doesn't care for your
respect for rules or norms.

00:10:41.506 --> 00:10:43.075
In fact, there's only one thing

00:10:43.075 --> 00:10:46.044
Trump does
seem to deeply care about.

00:10:46.044 --> 00:10:47.479
-Rich guys, they love rockets.

00:10:47.479 --> 00:10:49.148
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:52.785
[ Cheers and applause ]

